; SW-18 / ESH-0105 regression, promoted from tests/vm_parity/found/ once fixed.
;
; FILED (now FIXED): an exact bignum division that does not divide evenly lost
; exactness on the VM.  Native carried a bignum numerator through the rational
; tower; the VM's VmRational was int64/int64, so it could not represent the
; result and fell back to the correctly-rounded double:
;   native -r : 1267650600228229401496703205376/3
;   vm        : 4.2255020007607644e+29
;
; VmRational is bignum-capable now (is_big / big_num / big_den, mirroring the
; native eshkol_rational_t), so both engines print the exact value.  The wider
; class — bignum denominators, int64 overflow with no bignum operand at all,
; exact comparison of values that share a flonum — is gated by
; corpus/60_exact_bignum_rational.esk.
(display (/ (expt 2 100) 3))
(newline)
